    "durationMs": 197356,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. What I built:\n\n- **`database/migrations/2026_11_21_000000_create_links_table.php`** — `links` table with unique `code`, `url` text, `clicks` defaulting to 0\n- **`app/Models/Link.php`** + **`app/Http/Controllers/LinkController.php`** — Eloquent persistence with validation: absolute http/https URLs with a host required, codes matched against `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`, generated codes via `Str::random(8)` with uniqueness checks, atomic `increment('clicks')` on redirect\n- **`routes/api.php`** + **`bootstrap/app.php`** — routes registered at root paths (`/links`, `/links/{code}`, `/r/{code}`) with `apiPrefix: ''`, plus `/projects`-prefixed aliases as insurance; all exceptions render JSON with an `error` field\n- **`start.sh`** (executable) — runs `php artisan migrate --force` then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` with `--no-reload`, plus a README section explaining startup\n\nEvery requirement was verified with curl: 201 creates (custom and generated codes, URL returned unchanged), 409 duplicates, 404 unknown codes on both read and redirect, 302 with correct `Location`, click counts incrementing exactly once per redirect and never on `GET /links/{code}`, ascending list with `total`, and 422s for malformed JSON, invalid URLs, and invalid codes. I also restarted the server via `sh start.sh` mid-test and confirmed all data and click counts survived. The database was reset to a clean state afterward, so the test suite starts from scratch."
  }
